Translation patch: `HandshakePacket` (`MyDeserialize`, `MySerialize`, `new`, `into_owned`, the accessors, `nonce`)

Change:
  - Combinators become `match`es: `buf.parse(len).map(Some)?`, `opt.map(RawBytes::new)`, `opt.map(|x| x.into_owned())`, `opt.as_ref().map(|x| x.as_bytes())`, `opt.as_ref().map(|x| x.as_str())`, `opt.as_ref().map(|x| f(x)).unwrap_or_default()` (the default `u8` is 0).
  - Slice patterns `[head @ .., 0] => .., all => ..` (in `deserialize` and `auth_plugin`) become `if len > 0 && all[len - 1] == 0 { .. &all[..len - 1] .. } else { .. all .. }`; `split_last()` with `Some((0_u8, rest))` in `nonce` becomes the same test.
  - `auth_plugin`: `ParseBuf(name).parse_unchecked(()).expect("infallible")` becomes `AuthPlugin::from_bytes(name)`.
  - `scramble_1_ref`: `self.scramble_1.as_ref()` becomes `&self.scramble_1[..]`; `nonce`: `Vec::from(slice)` becomes `slice.to_vec()`, and the `if let Some(scramble_2)` that appends it moves into a private method `nonce_scramble_2()` returning the (trimmed) bytes, or an empty slice for `None`, which `nonce` appends unconditionally.
  - `new`: `scramble_2` and the length byte computed from it (`x.len() as u8`, or 0) are computed together in one `match` before the struct literal.
  - `serialize`: the auth-plugin-data length byte is computed by a new free function `handshake_auth_plugin_data_len(client_plugin_auth, &self.scramble_2)`, and the two trailing `if let Some(..)` writes move into a free function `serialize_handshake_tail(&self.scramble_2, &self.auth_plugin_name, buf)` that writes them in tail position (`serialize_handshake_auth_plugin_name`).
Why: Aeneas fails on closures and constructors used as values (patch 09), slice patterns (patch 06), `expect` on `io::Result` (`Debug for io::Error`), `AsRef for [T; N]`, `From<&[T]> for Vec<T>` (patch 58) and `split_last` are not modelled, and it fails ("Could not match the contexts" / "Unreachable") on joins after an `if`/`match` that borrows `self` in `serialize`, `nonce` and `new`.
Behaviour: Identical. Each `match` is the definition of the combinator; the slice-pattern and `split_last` rewrites test exactly the same condition; `AuthPlugin`'s parse is `Ok(from_bytes(name))` (see patch 62), so `expect` never panics; `to_vec` is `Vec::from` for slices; appending an empty slice is a no-op; the helpers compute and write the same values in the same order.

